      "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #63183\n\n`/v1/responses` responses with `\"status\": \"completed\"` never carried `completed_at`, so OpenAI-SDK clients reading `response.completed_at` always got `None`. The OpenAI Response object defines `completed_at` as the Unix timestamp (seconds) of completion, present when `status` is `completed`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `ResponsesResponse` gains `completed_at: int | None` (default `None`).\n- `ResponsesResponse.from_request()` sets `completed_at=int(time.time())` when `status == \"completed\"`, else `None`.\n- `from_request` is the single construction point for completed responses, so all paths are covered: non-streaming final responses (`serving.py` ~L929) and background completion flows build their final objects through it, while background initial (`\"queued\"`, ~L546) and streaming initial (`\"in_progress\"`, ~L1381) constructions keep `None` automatically. The only in-place status mutation on stored responses is the `\"failed\"` transition (`serving.py` L1120), where `completed_at` correctly stays `None`.\n- Invariant: `completed_at >= created_at` always holds — `from_request` is invoked when the response finishes, so the current time is the completion time while `created_time` was captured at creation.\n\n## Validation\n\nUnit tests (`tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_responses_completed_at.py`, CPU-only, no model weights or GPU needed):\n\n- `status=\"completed\"` → `completed_at` is not `None` and `>= created_at`\n- `status in {queued, in_progress, failed, cancelled}` → `completed_at` is `None`\n\nRepro from the issue against a served model now behaves as expected:\n\n```sh\ncurl -s http://localhost:8000/v1/responses -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"model\":\"<model>\",\"input\":\"Reply with the single word: ok\",\"store\":false}' \\\n  | jq -c '{status, created_at, has_completed_at: has(\"completed_at\")}'\n# {\"status\":\"completed\",\"created_at\":<t>,\"has_completed_at\":true}\n```\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: `ResponsesResponse` (protocol.py) carried `created_at` and `status` but never defined `completed_at`, and the single `from_request` constructor had no completion timestamp to set. The fix adds the field and populates it at that single point rather than threading timestamps through three call sites, keeping background/streaming initial states correct by construction.\n\n## AI assistance\n\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n🤖 This PR was produced autonomously by **novus**, a self-evolving agent federation (https://github.com/RexHuang/novus): root cause analysis, fix, unit tests, and this description were all agent-authored. Human supervision: RexHuang.\n\n## Pull Request Checklist\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimal impact — one new optional field plus one assignment at the single completed-response construction point; reuses existing pydantic field style.\n\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** New unit test file; CPU-only; also matches the issue's E2E repro contract (`completed_at >= created_at`, `has(\"completed_at\")` true).\n\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Follows surrounding field style (pydantic `Field` with description); keeps the constructor single-point so no per-call-site changes are needed.\n\n\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63783?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-au